hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"939","Zakaria bin Yahya bin Iyas told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muhajir told us, on the authority of Urwa bin Ruwaym, on the authority of Ibn Al-Dailami, who lived in Jerusalem, said that he stayed in search of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas in Medina, and asked about him. They said: He had He walked to Mecca, and he followed him and found that he had walked to Taif, so he followed him and found him in an area of land walking, fighting a man from the Quraysh, and the Qurayshi was committing adultery. With wine, when I met him, I greeted him and he greeted me. He said: Except for you today, and where did you come from? So I told him, then I asked him: Have you heard, O Abdullah bin Amr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Did he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, mention anything about drinking alcohol? He said: Yes, so Al-Qurashi took his hand, then went and said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No man from my nation drinks alcohol.” Then his forty morning prayer will be accepted.”"
